## Hints for Future Agents
Claude Code ignores defaultMode: "auto" when it comes from project
(.claude/settings.json) or local (.claude/settings.local.json) settings. It is
honored only in user or managed settings. This repo's claude_settings.json is
symlinked to ~/.claude/settings.json by install.sh:55, which is the user
location, so auto takes effect. Do not copy this file into a project's
.claude/ directory and expect auto to work.

skipDangerousModePermissionPrompt: true is still in the file and was left
alone deliberately. It no longer affects startup now that the default mode is
auto, but it still applies when launching with --dangerously-skip-permissions.

